hello from Westminster on the agenda  today we've got Prime Minister's  Questions coming up it's hard to predict  what the questions will be but no doubt  there'll be some mention of the Ofsted  report that's out today that looks into  how councils are coping with mechanisms  for dealing with child abuse and the  report finds that there's a lack of  leadership and poor planning despite the  fact that statutory guidance was  introduced five years ago many councils  have only just begun looking at this  problem and so the recommendations are  that they get their guidance in place  publish it and implement it also later  in the Commons today we're going to have  another debate on the European Arrest  Warrant but specific to the warrant  itself which has been called by Labour  because of what happened last week when  there was debate on the subject without  actually specifically mentioning the  warrant itself this is an effort to  embarrass the Conservatives and to  perhaps get some of those rebels from  the back benches out they are being  encouraged not to attend this debate so  we'll see what happens there but of  course the big political happening today  is the last day of electioneering and  campaigning in rochester and strood  before the big vote tomorrow
 

